[5] Creative proof target
  Proposed exposure theorem:
    Every primitive LRC14 source packet either has a q-witness, is one of
    the AP/GW taut boundary atoms, exposes a positive Haar bridge with a
    familywise Fejer interval certificate, or carries a labelled K33/petal
    handoff whose state-lift theorem discharges it.

  In this audit:
    non-AP/GW zero-safe rows=0
    hard Fejer-margin rows=18
  The missing global lemma is not another scalar invariant.  It is a
  no-hidden-kernel lemma: once the packet labels are retained, the only
  zero-open kernel is AP/GW, and every positive packet has a uniform
  interval-certificate assembly path.

  Suggested next formal sublemma:
    q>=14 and non-AP/GW source packets have either a positive endpoint
    bridge whose largest component supports a Fejer certificate before
    the first invisible speed, or a named K33/C27 state-lift label.
